    <string name="guide_title">Setup from your phone</string>
    <string name="guide_intro">No computer needed. Follow these steps on an Android phone near the router.</string>
    <string name="guide_step1_title">Connect to HappVPN Wi-Fi</string>
    <string name="guide_step1_body">Join the HappVPN network in phone Wi-Fi settings. If Android says there is no internet, choose Stay connected. The app reaches the router only on the same local network.</string>
    <string name="guide_step2_title">Check the router address</string>
    <string name="guide_step2_body">The default address is 192.168.1.1. If it does not connect, find Gateway in the phone Wi-Fi details, enter that address on the main screen and tap Connect. Another router will fail the security check.</string>
    <string name="guide_step3_title">Pair the phone once</string>
    <string name="guide_step3_body">Enter the router admin password in Pair phone on the main screen. The password is not saved. Tap Refresh after pairing.\n\nIf SSH password login is disabled, copy the public key below. In the router web interface open System → Administration → SSH-Keys, paste the key and tap Add key. Then return and tap Refresh. If you do not have the admin password, send the public key to someone who already has router access.</string>
    <string name="guide_copy_key">Copy public key</string>
    <string name="guide_router_page">Router page</string>
    <string name="guide_step4_title">Add a VPN subscription</string>
    <string name="guide_step4_body">Paste one or two HTTPS subscription URLs on the main screen and tap Get servers. All Shadowsocks servers appear in one list. happ://crypt5, VLESS and Hysteria do not work on this router. Keep subscription URLs private.</string>
    <string name="guide_step5_title">Test and install</string>
    <string name="guide_step5_body">Tap Find and test best server. The app tests reachable servers through the router and chooses a fast working one. Choose the subscription expiry date, then tap Install all servers. You can also select a server manually.</string>
    <string name="guide_step6_title">Verify the VPN exit</string>
    <string name="guide_step6_body">Turn on VPN mode and tap Refresh. VPN is on and an Exit IP should appear. With automatic selection enabled, the router chooses the lowest-latency working server.</string>
    <string name="guide_troubleshoot_title">If a step fails</string>
    <string name="guide_troubleshoot_body">• Router not found: Check Wi-Fi and the gateway address.\n• Host key error: This IP belongs to another router. Connect to the right network.\n• Pairing failed: Check the password or use the SSH-Keys method.\n• Subscription will not load: Download profiles over mobile data, then return to HappVPN Wi-Fi before testing.\n• VPN test fails: Try another Shadowsocks server. The current connection stays unchanged.</string>
